# Collected telemetry. Written by the collector at the install path at runtime.
# These carry the machine name, the signed-in user and a running list of the
# processes they have open -- they do not belong in a repo, even a private one.
events.ndjson
perf.ndjson
data.js
perf.js
status.js
meta.js
state.json
collector.log

# Whole-folder guard in case someone clones or points the collector inside the
# repo rather than at C:\ProgramData\EndpointHealth.
EndpointHealth/data/
**/EndpointHealth-data/

# Browser "save as" duplicates. These are the reason a stale collector can keep
# running after what looks like a successful update -- never commit one.
*-1.ps1
*-2.ps1
*-1.html
*-2.html
*-1.md
* (1).*
* - Copy.*

# Perfmon binary logs, in case a .blg is ever dropped next to the scripts.
*.blg
*.etl

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
